              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9708004"} arXiv:hep-th/9708004
          %div
            %h3#ReferencesIdentificationOfYangMillsMonopolesWithRationalMaps Identification of Yang-Mills monopoles with rational maps
            %p
              The following lists references concerned with the identification of the (extended)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+Yang-Mills+monopoles"} moduli space of Yang-Mills monopoles
              (in the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+state"} BPS limit
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higgs+field"} Higgs
              potential) with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+space"} mapping space
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+maps"} rational maps
              from the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+plane"} complex plane
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+maps"} holomorphic maps
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+sphere"} Riemann sphere
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}P^1
              (at infinity in
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^3
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SU%282%29"} SU(2)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flag+variety"} flag variety
              such as (see
              %a{:href => "#IonnadouSutcliffe99a"} Ionnadou &amp; Sutcliffe 1999a
              for review) to a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset+space"} coset space
              by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+torus"} maximal torus
              (for maximal
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetry+breaking"} symmetry breaking
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+projective+space"} complex projective space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}P^{n-1}
              (for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SU%28n%29"} SU(n)
              and minimal symmetry breaking).
            %p
              The identification was
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjecture"} conjectured
              (following an analogous result for
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+instantons"} Yang-Mills instantons
            %ul
              %li#Atiyah84
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Atiyah"}> Michael Atiyah
                , Section 5 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Instantons in two and four dimensions
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01212288"} doi:10.1007/BF01212288
            %p
              Full understanding of the rational map involved as “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scattering"} scattering
              data” of the monopole is due to:
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacques+Hurtubise"}> Jacques Hurtubise
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Monopoles and rational maps: a note on a theorem of Donaldson
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/communications-in-mathematical-physics/volume-100/issue-2/Monopoles-and-rational-maps--a-note-on-a-theorem/cmp/1103943443.full"} euclid:cmp/1103943443
            %p
              The identification with (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"}> pointed
              )
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+functions"} holomorphic functions
              out of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+sphere"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℂ
                      %msup
                        %mi P
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}P^1
              was proven…
            %p
              …for the case of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SU%282%29"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SU
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2)
              (maps to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+sphere"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℂ
                      %msup
                        %mi P
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}P^1
              itself) in
            %ul
              %li#Donaldson84
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simon+Donaldson"}> Simon Donaldson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Nahm’s Equations and the Classification of Monopoles
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1103941858"} euclid:cmp.1103941858
            %p
              …for the more general case of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+Lie+group"} classical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
              with maximal symmetry breaking (maps to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset+space"} coset space
              by the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+torus"} maximal torus
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacques+Hurtubise"}> Jacques Hurtubise
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em The classification of monopoles for the classical groups
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01260389"} doi:10.1007/BF01260389
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacques+Hurtubise"}> Jacques Hurtubise
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+K.+Murray"} Michael K. Murray
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em On the construction of monopoles for the classical groups
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/communications-in-mathematical-physics/volume-122/issue-1/On-the-construction-of-monopoles-for-the-classical-groups/cmp/1104178316.full"} euclid:cmp/1104178316
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Murray"}> Michael Murray
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Stratifying monopoles and rational maps
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01228347"} doi:10.1007/BF01228347
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacques+Hurtubise"}> Jacques Hurtubise
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+K.+Murray"} Michael K. Murray
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Monopoles and their spectral data
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/communications-in-mathematical-physics/volume-133/issue-3/Monopoles-and-their-spectral-data/cmp/1104201504.full"} euclid:cmp/1104201504
            %p
              … for the fully general case of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semisimple+Lie+groups"} semisimple
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+groups"} gauge groups
              with any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetry+breaking"} symmetry breaking
              (maps to any
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flag+varieties"} flag varieties
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stuart+Jarvis"}> Stuart Jarvis
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Euclidian Monopoles and Rational Maps
                  %strong 77
                  1 (1998) 170-192 (
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1112/S0024611598000434"}> doi:10.1112/S0024611598000434
                  )
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stuart+Jarvis"}> Stuart Jarvis
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Construction of Euclidian Monopoles
                  %strong 77
                  1 (1998) (
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1112/S0024611598000446"}> doi:10.1112/S0024611598000446
                  )
            %p and for un-pointed maps in
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stuart+Jarvis"}> Stuart Jarvis
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A rational map of Euclidean monopoles via radial scattering
                %strong 524
                (2000) 17-41(
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1515/crll.2000.055"}> doi:10.1515/crll.2000.055
                )
            %p Further discussion:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+P.+Boyer"}> Charles P. Boyer
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B.+M.+Mann"} B. M. Mann
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      Monopoles, non-linear
                      = succeed "-models," do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi σ
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01224128"} arXiv:10.1007/BF01224128
              %li#IonnadouSutcliffe99a
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theodora+Ioannidou"}> Theodora Ioannidou
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Sutcliffe"} Paul Sutcliffe
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Monopoles and Harmonic Maps
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9903183"} arXiv:hep-th/9903183
              %li#IonnadouSutcliffe99b
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theodora+Ioannidou"}> Theodora Ioannidou
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Sutcliffe"} Paul Sutcliffe
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Monopoles from Rational Maps
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9905066"} arXiv:hep-th/9905066
            %p Review:
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+B.+Atanasov"}> Alexander B. Atanasov
                ,
                %em Magnetic monopoles and the equations of Bogomolny and Nahm
                (
                %a{:href => "http://abatanasov.com/Files/3D%20Monopoles.pdf"}> pdf
                ), chapter 5 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Magnetic Monopoles, ‘t Hooft Lines, and the Geometric Langlands Correspondence
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://abatanasov.com/Files/Thesis.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://abatanasov.com/Files/Thesis%20Presentation.pdf"} slides
            %p
              On the relevant
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+of+rational+maps"} homotopy of rational maps
              (see there for more references):
            %ul
              %li#Segal79
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"}> Graeme Segal
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The topology of spaces of rational functions
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.acta/1485890033"} euclid:1485890033
          %h3#as_transversal_ddbrane_intersections
            As transversal D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            \/D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi p
                  %mo +
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p+2)
            \-brane intersections
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+monopoles"} Yang-Mills monopoles
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+engineering+of+QFT"} geometrically engineeted
            as transversally
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+brane"} intersecting
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dp-D%28p%2B2%29-brane+bound+states"} Dp-D(p+2)-brane bound states
          %p
            For transversal
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D1-D3-brane+bound+states"} D1-D3-brane bound states
          %ul
            %li#Diaconescu97
              %p
                Duiliu-Emanuel Diaconescu,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em D-branes, Monopoles and Nahm Equations
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9608163"} arxiv:hep-th/9608163
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Amihay+Hanany"}> Amihay Hanany
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Type IIB Superstrings, BPS Monopoles, And Three-Dimensional Gauge Dynamics
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9611230"} arxiv:hep-th/9611230
            %li
              %p
                Jessica K. Barrett, Peter Bowcock,
                %em Using D-Strings to Describe Monopole Scattering
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0402163"}> arxiv:hep-th/0402163
                )
            %li
              %p
                Jessica K. Barrett, Peter Bowcock,
                %em Using D-Strings to Describe Monopole Scattering - Numerical Calculations
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0512211"}> arxiv:hep-th/0512211
                )
          %p
            For transversal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D2-D4+brane+intersections"} D2-D4 brane intersections
            (with an eye towards
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FQCD"} AdS/QCD
          %ul
            %li
              Alexander Gorsky, Valentin Zakharov, Ariel Zhitnitsky,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On Classification of QCD defects via holography
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0902.1842"} arxiv:0902.1842
          %p
            For transversal
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D3-D5+brane+intersections"} D3-D5 brane intersections
          %ul
            %li#GaiottoWitten08
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Davide+Gaiotto"}> Davide Gaiotto
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
              = succeed "," do
                %em Supersymmetric Boundary Conditions in N=4 Super Yang-Mills Theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0804.2902"} arXiv:0804.2902
          %p
            For transversal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-D8-brane+intersections"} D6-D8-brane intersections
            (with an eye towards
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FQCD"} AdS/QCD
          %ul
            %li#HLPY08
              Deog Ki Hong, Ki-Myeong Lee, Cheonsoo Park, Ho-Ung Yee, Section V of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Holographic Monopole Catalysis of Baryon Decay
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0804.1326"} https:arXiv:0804.1326
          %p
            With emphasis on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/half+NS5-branes"} half NS5-branes
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+I%27+string+theory"} type I' string theory
          %ul
            %li#HananyZaffaroni99
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Amihay+Hanany"}> Amihay Hanany
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alberto+Zaffaroni"} Alberto Zaffaroni
              = succeed "," do
                %em Monopoles in String Theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9911113"} arxiv:hep-th/9911113
          %p
            The moduli space of monopoles appears also in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            on a complex surface (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AGT-correspondence"}> AGT-correspondence
            ):
          %ul
            %li
              Benjamin Assel,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sakura+Schafer-Nameki"} Sakura Schafer-Nameki
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  M5-branes on
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 2
                          %mo ×
                          %msub
                            %mi M
